# Git commit messages

When creating commits in this repository:

- Use a **single-line subject only** — **no commit body**
- Keep the subject **under 100 characters**
- Be professional and concise; focus on **why**
- Never add AI attribution trailers (`Co-Authored-By`, `Made with Cursor`, etc.)
- Split work into **multiple focused commits** when changes cover distinct concerns

## Examples

```text
Restore legacy Weebs access and drop weebs code placeholder.
Defer avatar saves until Save and restore themed presets.
Replace login native validation with shadcn Field errors.
```
